tion":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:9e601e00ab65aef2dc9b4eb230c913b2bd0ab173a66651d20ad161fb36a51570","file":"preprints/Random-subspace-tests-and-trace-smoothing-for-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":24,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"0c4d9147de9a55522701a635310b4ae0cb33760642a8955cbd7559304e56f440","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Random-subspace-tests-and-trace-smoothing-for-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9e601e00ab65aef2dc9b4eb230c913b2bd0ab173a66651d20ad161fb36a51570","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Random-subspace-tests-and-trace-smoothing-for-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L24"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{ten:lowplanes:main}\nThere is an absolute $P\\ge2$ such that for every dyadic $n\\ge2$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{ten:lowplanes:eq:1}\n \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\rm reg}|Q_n|^P\\le1+n^{-10}.\n\\end{equation}\nIf $v$ is an integer with $2v\\ge P$, then $v$ independent sweeps have total-variation distance at most $\\frac12n^{-5}$ from uniform, from every deterministic initial deck. Here $\\|\\mu-\\nu\\|_{\\rm TV}=\\tfrac12\\sum_g|\\mu(g)-\\nu(g)|$."}
